# Rank 1111 / CVE-2021-31405: Vaadin's EmailField validates input against a
# hand-written regex whose domain-suffix group backtracks catastrophically on
# crafted input, hanging the JVM thread that re-validates it (CWE-400).
#
# ATTENTION: engine gap. code.CatastrophicRegex / VYQL-DOS-003 exist, but every
# binding matches a literal substring of one known-vulnerable regex rather than
# nested-quantifier structure; there is no regex-AST or backtracking analysis.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1111: the domain-suffix group repeats an unescaped dot inside an unbounded class"
  lang java
  file EmailField.java
  reject_review code.CatastrophicRegex
  code
  ```
  package com.vaadin.flow.component.textfield;

  public class EmailField {
      private static final String EMAIL_PATTERN =
          "^[a-zA-Z0-9.!#$%&'*+/=?^_`{|}~-]+@[a-zA-Z0-9-]+(?:.[a-zA-Z0-9-]+)*$";

      public boolean isValid(String value) {
          return value.matches(EMAIL_PATTERN);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1111: the domain suffix is one dot literal and a bounded tail class"
  lang java
  file EmailField.java
  reject_review code.CatastrophicRegex
  code
  ```
  package com.vaadin.flow.component.textfield;

  public class EmailField {
      private static final String EMAIL_PATTERN = "^" + "([a-zA-Z0-9_\\.\\-+])+" // local
              + "@" + "[a-zA-Z0-9-.]+" // domain
              + "\\." + "[a-zA-Z0-9-]{2,}" // tld
              + "$";

      public boolean isValid(String value) {
          return value.matches(EMAIL_PATTERN);
      }
  }
  ```
